{%- comment -%}
  Why Wear Label. Brief §9.5.

  Four claims, and every one of them is checkable against something the studio
  has actually done — which is the only reason this section is allowed. The brief
  is explicit that the B2B portfolio is still small and that wording like "trusted
  by hundreds of companies" is not to be used, so the argument this section makes
  is about capability, not scale: the label has been developing and selling
  garments since 2020 (brief §13), it adapts pieces to what a client needs, it
  knows material, cutting and fit, and it runs the job end to end. None of those
  needs a client count to be true.

  If somebody adds a fifth card here, the test is the same one the service band
  carries: a claim that lives only in this section is a claim nobody has to keep.

  CREAM CARDS ON WHITE, not a cream band. The section directly above is a cream
  band with rules, and stacking a second cream band under it merges the two into
  one region. Cream on white is the theme's declared card pattern — the same
  treatment the review cards and the hero panel use — so this reads as four
  objects on the page rather than as another horizontal stripe.

  SPELLING. The brief writes "Customization"; the default below is
  "customisation", because this site is set in British spelling throughout
  ("Colourway" is a size-and-colour option name, a locale key and a filter
  label). One page spelled the other way is the kind of thing a reader notices
  without being able to say why. The setting is editable either way.
{%- endcomment -%}

<section aria-labelledby="why-heading" class="mx-auto w-full max-w-content px-gutter py-section">
  <div data-reveal class="flex flex-col gap-4">
    <h2 id="why-heading" class="text-h1 leading-h1">
      {% render 'copy', value: section.settings.heading, label: 'heading' %}
    </h2>

    {%- if section.settings.body != blank -%}
      <p class="wl-measure text-body leading-body text-ink-muted">{{ section.settings.body }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  <ul class="mt-block grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
    {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
      <li data-reveal class="flex flex-col gap-3 rounded-sm bg-canvas p-7" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
        <h3 class="text-h3 leading-h3 font-medium text-ink">
          {% render 'copy', value: block.settings.title, label: 'value' %}
        </h3>

        <p class="text-caption leading-snug text-ink-muted">
          {% render 'copy', value: block.settings.body, label: 'detail', lines: 3 %}
        </p>
      </li>
    {%- endfor -%}
  </ul>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Why Wear Label",
  "max_blocks": 6,
  "settings": [
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Every card has to be checkable against something the studio has actually done. This section argues capability, not scale — the brief rules out wording like 'trusted by hundreds of companies' while the portfolio is still small." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Why Wear Label" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "body", "label": "Intro" }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "value",
      "name": "Value",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "title", "label": "Title" },
        { "type": "textarea", "id": "body", "label": "Detail" }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Why Wear Label",
      "blocks": [
        { "type": "value", "settings": { "title": "Fashion experience", "body": "Wear Label has been developing and selling fashion products since 2020." } },
        { "type": "value", "settings": { "title": "Flexible customisation", "body": "Pieces are adapted to what the organisation actually needs." } },
        { "type": "value", "settings": { "title": "Product & fit understanding", "body": "Experience in apparel development, material, cutting and fit." } },
        { "type": "value", "settings": { "title": "End-to-end process", "body": "Consultation through production and delivery." } }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
